+
+### Menu OCR And Document Intelligence
+
+#### [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is one of the strongest document AI repositories on GitHub for turning images and PDFs into structured, AI-friendly data. The README highlights multilingual OCR, document parsing, JSON and Markdown export, key information extraction, table handling, and deep integration into broader document pipelines. For restaurants, it is especially valuable for digitizing menus, vendor catalogs, handwritten scans, training packets, and back-office PDFs. It is also practical when a team wants one toolkit that spans OCR, structure extraction, and downstream AI ingestion. GitHub shows around 66.5k stars, Python as the primary language, Apache-2.0 licensing, and active releases in November 2025.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+- **Stars:** 66.5k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Nov 13, 2025
+- **Category:** ocr, document-parsing
+- **Best for:** extracting structured menu and document data at scale
+
+---
+
+#### [Tesseract OCR](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract)
+> **Description:** Tesseract remains the most established open source OCR engine in this space. Its README explains support for more than 100 languages, multiple image formats, multiple output formats such as plain text, hOCR, PDF, TSV, ALTO, and PAGE, plus both classic and LSTM-based OCR modes. It is lower level than newer document AI stacks, but it is still a dependable foundation for menu scanning, printed signage extraction, and receipt or document processing when teams want maximum control. It is especially strong when paired with custom preprocessing and layout tooling. GitHub shows roughly 71.9k stars, C++ as the primary language, Apache-2.0 licensing, and activity on January 1, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract)
+- **Stars:** 71.9k ⭐
+- **Language:** C++
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Jan 1, 2026
+- **Category:** ocr, classic-ocr
+- **Best for:** reliable OCR pipelines for printed menus, receipts, and legacy scans
+
+---
+
+#### [docTR](https://github.com/mindee/doctr)
+> **Description:** docTR is a deep-learning OCR library focused on text detection and text recognition with an accessible Python interface. The README positions it as a seamless and high-performing library for OCR-related tasks, with modern model architectures and support for common deployment patterns. It is useful for restaurant teams that want better OCR than basic image-to-text extraction, especially when menu layouts vary or when document quality is inconsistent. Compared with end-to-end platforms, docTR is better as a building block inside custom pipelines. GitHub shows about 5.7k stars, Python as the main language, Apache-2.0 licensing, and a latest public release in July 2025.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/mindee/doctr](https://github.com/mindee/doctr)
+- **Stars:** 5.7k ⭐
