+
+#### [Unstructured](https://github.com/Unstructured-IO/unstructured)
+> **Description:** Unstructured is an open source ETL layer for transforming messy documents into structured data for language models. The README emphasizes partitioning, cleaning, chunking, and connecting documents to downstream LLM workflows, which is exactly the problem many restaurant groups face with SOPs, training files, catering packages, and menus spread across PDFs and office documents. It is less about OCR alone and more about building dependable ingestion pipelines. That makes it a good choice when restaurant teams need document normalization before search, RAG, or analytics. GitHub shows about 13.6k stars, HTML as the dominant GitHub language view, Apache-2.0 licensing, and activity on December 30, 2025.
+
