+- Include GitHub metadata:
+  - stars
+  - primary language
+  - license
+  - recent activity date
+
+## Recommended Pull Request Format
+
+Please include:
+
+1. Repository name
+2. GitHub URL
+3. Category suggestion
+4. 2-4 sentence summary
+5. Why it is useful for restaurants
+6. Stars, language, license, and last commit date
+
+## Quality Bar
+
+- Check that the repository still exists and is public.
+- Do not submit duplicates.
+- If a project has mixed or unusual licensing, note that explicitly.
+- If a category is still thin, it is better to document the gap honestly than to force unrelated tools into it.
+
+## Style Notes
+
+- Keep descriptions factual.
+- Prefer mature or actively maintained repositories.
+- Restaurant-adjacent infrastructure is acceptable when the use case is concrete, such as menu OCR, support automation, forecasting, or retrieval.
