+
+# Best AI Tools for Restaurants 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-restaurants-2026?style=social)
+
+> The best AI tools for restaurants 2026 are not a single POS plugin or hype-filled SaaS dashboard. They are practical open source building blocks you can self-host from GitHub for menu OCR, guest messaging, ordering flows, internal knowledge search, and demand forecasting. This list only includes tools that exist as public GitHub repositories and are relevant to real restaurant operations.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `TastyIgniter` is the strongest restaurant-native OSS platform here if you need online ordering, reservations, and restaurant management in one stack.
+- `Chatwoot`, `Rasa`, `Pipecat`, `Flowise`, and `Langflow` are the best starting points for AI-assisted guest support, ordering flows, and front-desk automation.
+- `PaddleOCR`, `Tesseract`, `Surya`, `Marker`, and `Unstructured` are the most useful menu digitization and document-to-structured-data tools.
+- `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, `Haystack`, and `LanceDB` are strong foundations for menu search, internal SOP retrieval, and recommendation systems.
+- `Prophet`, `Darts`, `StatsForecast`, and `MLForecast` are the most practical OSS options for demand forecasting, labor planning, and prep optimization.
+
+## Why This List
+Restaurants need AI tools that can survive bad menu PDFs, multilingual guests, messy operational documents, and demand swings across dayparts. Open source matters here because restaurants, franchise groups, and agencies often need self-hosting, source visibility, and the freedom to tailor workflows around ordering, reservations, kitchens, and support.
+
+There is also a real market gap: truly restaurant-native open source AI products are still limited on GitHub. To stay honest, this list mixes restaurant-specific repositories with adjacent OSS AI infrastructure that restaurants can deploy today for menu extraction, conversational ordering, forecasting, retrieval, and workflow automation.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Restaurant Ops And Guest Experience
+
+#### [TastyIgniter](https://github.com/tastyigniter/TastyIgniter)
+> **Description:** TastyIgniter is the clearest restaurant-specific foundation in this list. Its README positions it as a developer-friendly, open source platform for online ordering, table reservation, and restaurant management, aimed at helping offline restaurants and takeaway businesses reach online customers. It is customizable, extension-driven, and suited to multi-location deployments. While it is not an LLM framework by itself, it is the most relevant OSS operating layer to pair with AI features such as menu extraction, support chat, and forecasting. GitHub shows roughly 3.3k stars, PHP as the primary language, an MIT license, and activity on September 12, 2025.
