+> **Description:** StatsForecast focuses on fast, scalable statistical and econometric forecasting models such as AutoARIMA, ETS, CES, Theta, and MSTL. The README stresses production scale, efficient implementations, distributed execution support, probabilistic forecasting, and exogenous variables. Restaurants can use it when they need a lot of forecasts quickly across stores, dayparts, categories, or SKUs, and when classical models are still the right operational baseline. It is particularly appealing for prep and purchasing use cases where speed and coverage across many series matter more than flashy interfaces. GitHub shows a healthy community, Python as the primary language, Apache-2.0 licensing, and activity in late 2025.
